Third party material
--------------------

ItemTree_Data/Data/generated/EraSources.lua and ItemTree_Data/Data/generated/BossLoot.lua (in
the ItemTree_Data folder, which a release ships beside ItemTree). These two files are compiled from
the CMaNGOS Classic content database (github.com/cmangos/classic-db), which is licensed under the
GNU General Public License version 3, and hold data derived from it alone, so these two files alone
are distributed under GPL-3.0 rather than the terms above. The files beside them that the addon
joins them to, ItemTree_Data/Data/generated/EraPlaces.lua and
ItemTree_Data/Data/generated/BossLootIndex.lua, hold ItemTree's own data (the zone names, maps,
pins and sides, and the places and their bosses) and fall under the terms above. Both also read pfQuest's vanilla database (github.com/shagu/pfQuest,
MIT licensed) for area ids and nothing else. The full GPL-3.0 text is in LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt and
CMaNGOS's own copyright notice is in LICENSES/cmangos-COPYRIGHT.md. The source they are compiled
from, and the scripts that compile them, are at
https://github.com/Rockjaw-Bonesnapper-Co/itemtree-era-sources.

Libs/LibStub. Placed in the public domain by its authors, as its own file header says. Not
committed to this repository; a packaged release embeds it.

Libs/CallbackHandler-1.0. An Ace3 library under the Ace3 licence, a BSD style licence:
redistribution is permitted while the copyright notice, the conditions and the disclaimer are kept,
a stand alone release of the library is prohibited without prior written authorisation from the
Lead of the Ace3 Development Team, and the Ace3 name may not be used to endorse anything derived
from it. The full text is in LICENSES/Ace3.txt. Not committed to this repository.

Blizzard's material. World of Warcraft, its item, creature, quest and zone names, the numbers
behind them, and every texture ItemTree draws by in-client path or atlas name belong to Blizzard
Entertainment, Inc. ItemTree ships no Blizzard artwork and claims no ownership of Blizzard's data.
